developer.name = "Akshay";
developer.employeeId = 101;

developer.work();
developer.writeCode();


Developer gets name, employeeId, and work() from Employee.


3. Polymorphism


Polymorphism means one interface or reference can represent different implementations 
and the same method call can behave differently depending on the actual object. In Java, runtime polymorphism is achieved through method overriding, 
while compile-time polymorphism is achieved through method overloading.

class Employee {

    void work() {
        System.out.println("Employee is working");
    }
}

class Developer extends Employee {

    @Override
    void work() {
        System.out.println("Developer is writing code");
    }
}


