    @Override
    void work() {
        System.out.println("Manager is managing the team");
    }
}

Employee employee1 = new Developer();
Employee employee2 = new Manager();

employee1.work();
employee2.work();



4. Abstraction : 

Abstraction means exposing essential behavior while hiding implementation details. 
In Java, we commonly achieve it using interfaces and abstract classes.
For example, a PaymentService interface can expose a pay() method while different implementations handle UPI or credit-card processing internally.




